Subject: [PATCH 07157/11362] [outer-loop] exp5709 n=3: fair sample-size rerun,
 Ternary Bonsai 0/3 vs 9B's 1/3 (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5599-3)

Operator caught a real methodology gap: exp5709's n=1 result (0/1) was being
compared against exp5599's 9B baseline at n=3 (1/3) -- not apples-to-apples.
A single 0/1 draw is statistically uninformative on its own (67% likely by
chance even if the true rate matched the 9B's ~33%).

Re-ran at n_repeats=3 to match the 9B's sample size exactly. Cheap since
Ternary Bonsai runs fast on the real 3090 (~213s/attempt). Real result: all
three draws reached a level-up and replicated the IDENTICAL failure shape
(round 1 produces valid code, rejected as degenerate_goal_predicate, every
time; round 2 refactor fails every time) -- mean_reinduce_duration_s=168.8,
plan_rate_given_levelup=0/3=0.0.

This is now the real apples-to-apples comparison: Ternary Bonsai 0/3 vs the
frozen 9B's 1/3, same sample size. The 3/3 identical failure reproduction
also sharpens the finding beyond what n=1 could show -- this is a
reproducible failure mode (systematically wrong goal predicate), not
stochastic noise. adversarial_verify.py clean. Frozen live-submission
generator remains unchanged.
